            {
              "id": "p16-q23-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "How many more cards less than 3 do you need to add so that the probability of getting a number less than 3 is 0.5? Show all your working.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "8 more cards.\n\nAdding $x$ favourable cards also increases the total: solve $\\frac{6+x}{20+x}=\\frac12$.",
          "worked": "The scale shows a probability of $0.3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Cards less than 3}&=0.3\\times20\\\\\\text{Cards less than 3}&=6\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe initial probability is $\\frac{6}{20}$. Let $x$ be the number of cards less than 3 added.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{6+x}{20+x}&=\\frac{1}{2}\\\\2(6+x)&=20+x\\\\12+2x&=20+x\\\\x&=8\\end{align*}$$\n\nAdd 8 cards.\n\nCheck:\n$$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{less than }3)&=\\frac{6+8}{20+8}\\\\P(\\text{less than }3)&=\\frac{14}{28}\\\\P(\\text{less than }3)&=\\frac{1}{2}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q23-root-bank-p16-q23-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "After making the probability 0.5, Ally adds 3 cards numbered less than 3. How many cards numbered 3 or more must she also add to keep the probability at 0.5?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "3 cards.",
          "worked": "After part (a), there are 14 cards of each kind. Adding 3 cards of each kind keeps the counts equal: $\\frac{17}{34}=0.5$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p16-q23-root-bank-p16-q23-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "How many cards are now in the collection?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "34 cards.",
          "worked": "$20+8+3+3=34$ cards.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 8
      }
    ]
  },
